```c
void acquire(atomic_int *lock) {
    int expected = 0;
    while (!atomic_compare_exchange_weak(lock, &expected, 1)) expected = 0;
}
void release(atomic_int *lock) { atomic_store(lock, 0); }
```

Correctness rests on CAS being **atomic**: the check-and-set happens as one indivisible operation, so if two threads race, exactly one CAS succeeds and every other fails and retries — no window where both believe they won. Release needs no atomic op — only the holder ever writes it.

Trade-off: this spins (burns CPU), fine only for short expected waits.

**Testing:** writing correct atomic code and explaining *why* it's correct.
